  "description": "MAWTEK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H112 O22 Pr4,C7 H8. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr1A (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr2A (Pr) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.889-4.012 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.37-108.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C150H112O22Pr4·C7H8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
